    "result": "I added `Add`, `Remove` and `Free` to `intervals.go` and fixed `Normalize`, but none of it has been compiled or tested. Both shells asked for approval to run `go test`, so I checked every case by tracing it by hand.\n\n`Normalize` had four bugs:\n- It sorted the caller's slice in place.\n- It did not merge intervals that touch (it compared with `\u003c`, not `\u003c=`).\n- A contained interval cut the End short. For example, {1,10} plus {2,4} gave {1,4}.\n- It kept empty and inverted intervals.\n\nIt now copies only the valid intervals, then sorts and merges with `max`. `Add` works on a copy of the input, so it cannot write into the caller's spare capacity. `Remove` and `Free` read the input only through `Normalize`, so they cannot change it either. The tests in `intervals_test.go` cover each operation, plus a check that the input slice stays unchanged.\n\n**TLDR**\nAll four operations are written with tests, but nothing has been run. Run `go test ./...` to confirm.",
